  "body": "Seen by the contributor while testing #482 (#339 slice 4) on a macOS release build (2026-11-09).\n\n**Today:** at a normal properties-pane width, each fixture row on the Fixtures page draws its name, position (\"0.00, 0…\"), \"y\" and the Unmark and Delete buttons on one horizontal line, and they clip off the pane's right edge. The \"Fixed (does not tu…\" checkbox is truncated. The per-fixture `place` row (x y z yaw Apply) has three unlabelled number boxes, and the contributor could not find it. They ended up on the model page, which correctly refuses to move a fixture (\"the Fixtures page places it\").\n\n**Expected:** the row wraps or stacks so every control is visible at the default pane width. The place fields are labelled X / Y / Z, and the selected fixture's placement is easy to find.\n\n**Done means:** a UI test at the default dock width asserts every fixture row's controls lie inside the pane rect, and the place fields carry axis labels.",
